From 20118633cfb95ce5fe4c5d6471f56195f87a9adf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:57:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/39] frameworks: drop the framework-virtualization
 references

the com.android.virt apex is no longer installed on the gsi and the
virtualization sources are excluded from the manifest sync, so every
reference to them has to go:

- boot: the platform bootclasspath cannot resolve the virt fragment
  anymore. framework-virtualization classes are served statically via
  framework-non-updatable-unbundled-impl-libs.
- SystemServiceRegistry resolved VirtualizationFrameworkInitializer
  unconditionally during static initialisation and PackageManagerNative
  read BuildFlags.SUPPORT_AVF_ADVANCE_MULTITENANCY at runtime, so zygote
  died with NoClassDefFoundError while preloading
  android.app.SystemServiceRegistry. drop the registration and the
  multitenancy sourceDir block; the aiseal registration stays as it is
  already gated behind aisealHostApis().
- Android.bp, api/Android.bp: the impl library and the combined apis
  entry cannot resolve. the visibility grant stays; grants do not
  require the target to exist.
- api.go adds framework-virtualization to the non updatable modules
  list, which makes the generated all-modules-system-stubs reference
  framework-virtualization.stubs.system and fails soong analysis.
- services.core depends on AvfBuildFlags, which is defined in the
  excluded tree, so soong analysis of services.core.unboosted fails.
---
